{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender rigid body dynamics blender rigid body dynamics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","fileName":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Simulation and Grease Pencil]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Simulation and Grease Pencil","Rigid Body Fracture and Collision","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender rigid body dynamics blender rigid body dynamics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","fileName":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics","heading":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Rigid body dynamics simulate objects that move and collide while retaining their form. An active rigid body responds to the calculation, while a passive body participates as an unmoving collider such as a floor.\n\nThis is more efficient and appropriate than making a soft body artificially stiff. Initial position and rotation give the solver the starting conditions from which falling, impact, and bouncing develop.\n\nGress applies the same rigid-body idea to destruction: a model must first be fractured into pieces, then a collider and force can drive their motion. The result still needs suitable fragment shapes, timing, surfacing, and motion blur to read as a real collapse. See [[Rigid Body Fracture and Collision]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Simulation and Grease Pencil","Rigid Body Fracture and Collision","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender rigid body dynamics blender rigid body dynamics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","fileName":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Rigid Body Dynamics","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf]]\n[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Simulation and Grease Pencil","Rigid Body Fracture and Collision","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}